IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cr1-schedules`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART VIII -- MISCELLANEOUS: regulation 79 (the Minister's
-- agreements), regulations 82 to 84.1 (the elections and the Indian's self-employment income), regulation 86
-- (international agreements and common-law partners) and regulation 88 (the Social Insurance Number).
-- Regulation 85 (the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings) is in cr1-part8-mpe.l4 and regulation 87 (interest on
-- amounts owing to Her Majesty) in cr1-part8-interest.l4. Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- Regulations 80 and 81 are repealed. "Prescribed form" is read with the Act's definition of "prescribed" (the
-- core rule `s 2(1) — prescribed`: a form the Minister has authorized; fork F8). The Act's sections 10 to 14
-- (the elections and the self-employed earnings) belong to pieces cp1 and cp2 (out of range: sections 10 to 14).

§ `Regulations, Part VIII -- miscellaneous (regs 79 to 84.1, 86, 88)`

§§ `Regulation 79: agreements the Minister of National Revenue may make`

-- src:823 | 79 The Minister of National Revenue may, on behalf of the Government of Canada, enter into an agreement with
-- src:824 | (a) the government of a country other than Canada,
-- src:825 | (b) an international organization, or
-- src:826 | (c) the government of a province,
-- src:827 | for giving effect to the provisions of paragraph 6(2)(h) or 7(1)(e) or (f) of the Act.
@ref Reg 79 (src:823-827)
DECLARE `cr1 Party the Minister may make an agreement with under regulation 79` IS ONE OF
    `the government of a country other than Canada`
    `an international organization`
    `the government of a province`
    `any other party`

@ref Reg 79 (src:823-827)
DECLARE `cr1 Provision an agreement under regulation 79 gives effect to` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph 6(2)(h) of the Act`
    `paragraph 7(1)(e) of the Act`
    `paragraph 7(1)(f) of the Act`
    `any other provision`

-- 79 The Minister of National Revenue may, on behalf of the Government of Canada, enter into an agreement with (a)
-- the government of a country other than Canada, (b) an international organization, or (c) the government of a
-- province, for giving effect to the provisions of paragraph 6(2)(h) or 7(1)(e) or (f) of the Act.
@ref Reg 79 (src:823-827)
GIVEN party IS A `cr1 Party the Minister may make an agreement with under regulation 79`
      provision IS A `cr1 Provision an agreement under regulation 79 gives effect to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 79 — the Minister of National Revenue may enter into the agreement on behalf of the Government of Canada` party provision MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF party EQUALS `any other party` THEN FALSE
        IF provision EQUALS `any other provision` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Regulations 82 to 84.1: the elections`

-- 82 The election referred to in paragraph 11(2)(a) of the Act shall be made by filing with the Minister the form
-- prescribed therefor.
-- src:829 | 82 The election referred to in paragraph 11(2)(a) of the Act shall be made by filing with the Minister the form prescribed therefor.
@ref Reg 82 (src:829)
GIVEN `the form is filed with the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is one the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 82 — the election referred to in paragraph 11(2)(a) of the Act is made` `the form is filed with the Minister` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` MEANS
    `the form is filed with the Minister` AND (`s 2(1) — prescribed` `a form or the information to be given on a form` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` FALSE FALSE)

-- 83 An individual, to whom section 10 of the Act is not applicable because an election made by the individual
-- under section 11 of the Act has been approved by the Minister, may revoke the election by advising the Minister
-- thereof in writing.
-- src:830 | 83 An individual, to whom section 10 of the Act is not applicable because an election made by the individual pursuant to section 11 of the Act has been approved by the Minister, may revoke the election by advising the Minister thereof in writing.
@ref Reg 83 (src:830)
GIVEN `section 10 of the Act is not applicable to the individual because an election under section 11 of the Act has been approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual advises the Minister of the revocation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83 — the individual has revoked the election under section 11 of the Act` `section 10 of the Act is not applicable to the individual because an election under section 11 of the Act has been approved by the Minister` `the individual advises the Minister of the revocation in writing` MEANS
    `section 10 of the Act is not applicable to the individual because an election under section 11 of the Act has been approved by the Minister` AND `the individual advises the Minister of the revocation in writing`

-- 83.1 The election referred to in subsection 12(1.1) of the Act is made or revoked by providing the prescribed form
-- to an employer of the person.
-- src:831 | 83.1 The election referred to in subsection 12(1.1) of the Act is made or revoked by providing the prescribed form to an employer of the person.
@ref Reg 83.1 (src:831)
GIVEN `the form is provided to an employer of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is one the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83.1 — the election referred to in subsection 12(1.1) of the Act is made or revoked` `the form is provided to an employer of the person` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` MEANS
    `the form is provided to an employer of the person` AND (`s 2(1) — prescribed` `a form or the information to be given on a form` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` FALSE FALSE)

-- 83.2 The election referred to in subsection 13(1.1) of the Act is made or revoked by (a) filing the prescribed
-- form, together with the return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year, with the Minister within one
-- year from June 15 in the year following the year for which the return is filed; or (b) filing the prescribed form
-- with the Minister within one year from June 15 in the year following the year for which the return of the
-- person's self-employed earnings has been filed. Both paragraphs end on the same day: June 15 of the second year
-- after the year of the return (finding in NOTES.md).
-- src:832 | 83.2 The election referred to in subsection 13(1.1) of the Act is made or revoked by
-- src:833 | (a) filing the prescribed form, together with the return of the person’s self-employed earnings for the year, with the Minister within one year from June 15 in the year following the year for which the return is filed; or
-- src:834 | (b) filing the prescribed form with the Minister within one year from June 15 in the year following the year for which the return of the person’s self-employed earnings has been filed.
@ref Reg 83.2 (src:832-834)
GIVEN `the year for which the return of the person's self-employed earnings is filed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 83.2 — the last day for filing the form to make or revoke the election referred to in subsection 13(1.1) of the Act` `the year for which the return of the person's self-employed earnings is filed` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` (YMD (`the year for which the return of the person's self-employed earnings is filed` PLUS 1) 6 15) (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)

@ref Reg 83.2 (src:832-834)
GIVEN `the year for which the return of the person's self-employed earnings is filed` IS A NUMBER
      `the form is filed together with the return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is filed with the Minister after that return has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is one the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the form is filed with the Minister` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 83.2 — the election referred to in subsection 13(1.1) of the Act is made or revoked` `the year for which the return of the person's self-employed earnings is filed` `the form is filed together with the return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year` `the form is filed with the Minister after that return has been filed` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` `the day the form is filed with the Minister` MEANS
        (`the form is filed together with the return of the person's self-employed earnings for the year` OR `the form is filed with the Minister after that return has been filed`)
    AND (`s 2(1) — prescribed` `a form or the information to be given on a form` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` FALSE FALSE)
    AND `the day the form is filed with the Minister` AT MOST (`reg 83.2 — the last day for filing the form to make or revoke the election referred to in subsection 13(1.1) of the Act` `the year for which the return of the person's self-employed earnings is filed`)

-- 84 (1) An individual to whom subsection 13(3) of the Act applies for a year may elect to have the individual's
-- contributory salary and wages for the year included as self-employed earnings for the purposes of section 10 of
-- the Act by filing with the Minister the form prescribed therefor. (2) The form shall be filed by the individual
-- (a) with the individual's income tax return, or (b) if the income tax return has already been filed, with the
-- Minister, within one year from April 30th of the year following the year for which the individual so elects (the
-- time limit is read as governing (a) and (b) alike: fork F16).
-- src:835 | 84 (1) An individual to whom subsection 13(3) of the Act applies for a year may elect to have the individual’s contributory salary and wages for the year included as self-employed earnings for the purposes of section 10 of the Act by filing with the Minister the form prescribed therefor.
-- src:836 | (2) The form referred to in subsection (1) shall be filed by an individual
-- src:837 | (a) with his income tax return, or
-- src:838 | (b) if his income tax return has already been filed, with the Minister
-- src:839 | within one year from April 30th of the year following the year for which he so elects.
@ref Reg 84(1), 84(2) (src:835-839)
GIVEN `the year for which the individual elects` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 84(2) — the last day for filing the form` `the year for which the individual elects` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` (YMD (`the year for which the individual elects` PLUS 1) 4 30) (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)

@ref Reg 84(1), 84(2) (src:835-839)
GIVEN `subsection 13(3) of the Act applies to the individual for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year for which the individual elects` IS A NUMBER
      `the form is filed with the individual's income tax return, or with the Minister if the return has already been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is one the Minister has authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the form is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 84 — the individual's contributory salary and wages for the year are included as self-employed earnings` `subsection 13(3) of the Act applies to the individual for the year` `the year for which the individual elects` `the form is filed with the individual's income tax return, or with the Minister if the return has already been filed` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` `the day the form is filed` MEANS
        `subsection 13(3) of the Act applies to the individual for the year`
    AND `the form is filed with the individual's income tax return, or with the Minister if the return has already been filed`
    AND (`s 2(1) — prescribed` `a form or the information to be given on a form` `the form is one the Minister has authorized` FALSE FALSE)
    AND `the day the form is filed` AT MOST (`reg 84(2) — the last day for filing the form` `the year for which the individual elects`)

-- 84.1 For the purposes of paragraph 14(c) of the Act, in the case of an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act, the
-- extent of the income of the Indian for the year from self-employment on a reserve, as defined in the Indian Act,
-- is the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for that year. (out of range: section 14, piece cp1)
-- src:840 | 84.1 For the purposes of paragraph 14(c) of the Act, in the case of an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act, the extent of the income of the Indian for the year from self-employment on a reserve, as defined in the Indian Act, is the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for that year.
@ref Reg 84.1 (src:840)
GIVEN `the person is an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 84.1 — the extent of the income of the Indian for the year from self-employment on a reserve` `the person is an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act` `the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for the year` MEANS
    IF `the person is an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act`
    THEN JUST `the amount described in paragraph 14(a) of the Act for the year`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 86: the agreements of Schedule IX and common-law partners`

-- 86 The agreements referred to in Schedule IX, which were entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act for the
-- making of reciprocal arrangements relating to the administration or operation of the Act, shall, in order to
-- give full effect to the Act, be applied in Canada in a manner that extends to common-law partners the treatment
-- afforded to spouses. A common-law partner is the Act's: cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the relevant
-- time and having so cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year (the core rule).
-- src:856 | 86 The agreements referred to in Schedule IX, which were entered into under subsection 107(1) of the Act for the making of reciprocal arrangements relating to the administration or operation of the Act, shall, in order to give full effect to the Act, be applied in Canada in a manner that extends to common-law partners the treatment afforded to spouses.
@ref Reg 86 (src:856)
GIVEN `the country whose agreement is in question` IS A STRING
      `the person is cohabiting with the contributor in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the continuous cohabitation began` IS A DATE
      `the relevant time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 86 — the agreement is applied so that the person has the treatment afforded to a spouse` `the country whose agreement is in question` `the person is cohabiting with the contributor in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` `the day the continuous cohabitation began` `the relevant time` MEANS
        `Schedule IX — the country has an agreement referred to` `the country whose agreement is in question`
    AND `s 2(1) — a common-law partner of a contributor at a relevant time` `the person is cohabiting with the contributor in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` `the day the continuous cohabitation began` `the relevant time`

§§ `Regulation 88: the Social Insurance Number`

-- 88 (1) The Minister or the Minister of National Revenue may cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to an
-- individual who has not been assigned a Social Insurance Number. (2) The Minister or the Minister of National
-- Revenue may cause a Social Insurance Number Card to be issued to an individual to whom a Social Insurance
-- Number was caused to be assigned under subsection (1). Either Minister may: the rules take no Minister as input.
-- src:890 | 88 (1) The Minister or the Minister of National Revenue may cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to an individual who has not been assigned a Social Insurance Number.
@ref Reg 88(1) (src:890)
GIVEN `the individual has been assigned a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 88(1) — a Minister may cause a Social Insurance Number to be assigned to the individual` `the individual has been assigned a Social Insurance Number` MEANS
    NOT `the individual has been assigned a Social Insurance Number`

-- src:891 | (2) The Minister or the Minister of National Revenue may cause a Social Insurance Number Card to be issued to an individual to whom a Social Insurance Number was caused to be assigned under subsection (1).
@ref Reg 88(2) (src:891)
GIVEN `a Social Insurance Number was caused to be assigned to the individual under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 88(2) — a Minister may cause a Social Insurance Number Card to be issued to the individual` `a Social Insurance Number was caused to be assigned to the individual under subsection (1)` MEANS
    `a Social Insurance Number was caused to be assigned to the individual under subsection (1)`
